    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. Classification of Railway Services\n- **Group 'A':** Gazetted officers recruited through UPSC (ESE, Civil Services Examination, CMS for Doctors).\n- **Group 'B':** Gazetted officers promoted from Group 'C' through 70% Selection (now CBT) and 30% LDCE.\n- **Group 'C':** Non-gazetted supervisory, clerical, technical, and operational staff in Pay Levels 1 to 7 (Grade Pay 1800 to 4600).\n- *Note:* Erstwhile Group 'D' (GP 1800 / Level 1) was merged into Group 'C' following 6th and 7th CPC recommendations.\n\n### 2. Recruitment Agencies & Quotas\n- **Railway Recruitment Boards (RRBs):** Conduct computer-based tests for technical & non-technical popular categories (NTPC, JE, SSE, ALP, Paramedical).\n- **Railway Recruitment Cells (RRCs):** Conduct recruitment for Level 1 posts, sports quota, scout & guide quota, and cultural quota at the Zonal level.\n- **Compassionate Ground Appointments (CGA):**\n  - Extended to the widow/widower or dependent son/daughter/adopted child of a railway servant who dies in harness or is medically invalidated (total medical unfitness).\n  - Time Limit: Applications normally accepted within 5 years of death; GM has powers to condone delays up to 20 years with Railway Board approval.\n  - Priority I (dying due to accident on duty) > Priority II (dying of disease) > Priority III (medical invalidation).\n\n### 3. Central Training Institutes (CTIs) of Indian Railways\n| Institute | Location | Specialization |\n|---|---|---|\n| **NAIR** (National Academy of Indian Railways) | Vadodara | Apex training for Group A/B probationary and in-service officers |\n| **IRICEN** (IR Institute of Civil Engineering) | Pune | Track, bridges, formation, civil engineering works |\n| **IRISET** (IR Institute of Signal Engg & Telecom) | Secunderabad | Signalling, interlocking, telecom, networking, IT |\n| **IRIMEE** (IR Institute of Mech & Elec Engineering) | Jamalpur | Rolling stock, diesel/steam mechanics, workshops |\n| **IREET** (IR Institute of Electrical Engineering) | Nashik | Traction, locomotives, OHE, electrical systems |\n| **IRITM** (IR Institute of Transport Management) | Lucknow | Traffic, commercial, logistics, operations |\n| **JR RPF Academy** | Lucknow | Railway Protection Force officers and staff |\n\n### 4. Training Under Apprentices Act, 1961\n- Trade apprentices are engaged in railway workshops (Fitter, Welder, Machinist, Electrician).\n- Stipend paid as per central rates.\n- **20% horizontal reservation** is provided to Course Completed Act Apprentices (CCAAs) in direct recruitment to Level 1 posts, with 1/3rd weightage to NCVT marks in CBT.\n\n### 5. Annual Performance Appraisal Report (APAR) & SPARROW\n- Grading scale: 1 to 10 (1-4: Below Average, 5-6: Good, 7-8: Very Good, 9-10: Outstanding).\n- Reporting Officer -> Reviewing Officer -> Accepting Authority workflow.\n- Mandatory communication of APAR entries and full grading to the employee within 15 days; employee can submit representation within 15 days.\n- **SPARROW (Smart Performance Appraisal Report Recording Online Window):** Electronic filing system ensuring transparency, time-stamping, and zero delays.\n",
