    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. Seniority, Lien & Transfers\n- **Seniority of Direct Recruits:** Determined by merit list at RRB or marks obtained in initial training course at CTIs/ZRTIs.\n- **Lien:** A railway employee acquiring a permanent post acquires a lien on that post. Lien is suspended if appointed substantive in another permanent post, and terminated only upon substantive confirmation elsewhere.\n- **Inter-Railway Transfers:**\n  - *Own Request Transfer:* Allowed after completing initial lock-in period (usually 5 years). The employee goes to the bottom of the seniority list in the new railway.\n  - *Mutual Transfer:* Two employees exchange places. The senior employee takes the seniority of the junior employee in the new unit (bottom seniority between the two).\n\n### 2. Comprehensive Leave Rules (Railway Servants Liberalized Leave Rules)\n| Leave Type | Quantum / Entitlement | Maximum Accumulation | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **LAP** (Leave on Average Pay) | 30 days/year (15 on Jan 1, 15 on Jul 1) | 300 days | Encashment up to 300 days at retirement; 10 days during service with pass (max 60 days in career) |\n| **LHAP** (Leave on Half Average Pay) | 20 days/year (10 on Jan 1, 10 on Jul 1) | No limit | Can be commuted on medical certificate (2 LHAP = 1 Commuted Full Pay) |\n| **CL** (Casual Leave) | 8 days (office) / 10 days (line staff) | Zero (lapses Dec 31) | Not recognized as absence from duty; cannot combine with LAP/LHAP |\n| **Maternity Leave** | 180 days per delivery (< 2 surviving children) | N/A | Full pay, counts for increment and pension |\n| **Paternity Leave** | 15 days | N/A | For male staff with < 2 children; within 6 months of delivery |\n| **Child Care Leave (CCL)** | 730 days during entire service | N/A | For women & single male parents; 100% pay for first 365 days, 80% for next 365 days |\n| **Study Leave** | Up to 24 months (36 months for doctors) | N/A | Minimum 5 years service required, executing bond to serve 3 years |\n\n### 3. Railway Pass Rules & HRMS e-Pass\n- **Privilege Pass & PTO (Privilege Ticket Order):**\n  - Non-Gazetted staff: 1 set of Pass + 4 sets of PTO per year during first 5 years; 3 sets of Pass + 4 sets of PTO after 5 years.\n  - Gazetted staff (Group A & B): 6 sets of Passes + 4 sets of PTO per year from date of appointment.\n  - PTO allows purchase of ticket at 1/3rd of the total fare.\n- **Post-Retirement Complimentary Pass (PRCP):**\n  - Granted based on qualifying service (minimum 20 years). Group A & B: 3 sets/year; Group C: 2 sets/year.\n- **Widow Pass Scheme:** Available to spouse of deceased employee upon payment of nominal subscription.\n\n### 4. Hours of Employment Regulations (HOER)\nClassified under the Railways Act, 1989 and HOER Rules, 2005:\n1. **Intensive:** Work strenuous, continuous concentration (e.g., Section Controllers, Heavy Cabin Operators). Statutory limit: **42 hours/week** (average over 2 weeks). Periodic rest: **30 consecutive hours**.\n2. **Continuous:** Regular continuous duty (e.g., Station Masters, Loco Pilots, Clerks). Statutory limit: **54 hours/week**. Periodic rest: **30 consecutive hours**.\n3. **Essentially Intermittent (EI):** Work involves long periods of inaction (e.g., Gatemen on C-class gates, Waiting room attendants). Statutory limit: **72 or 60 hours/week** (48 hrs work + 12/24 hrs split). Periodic rest: **24 consecutive hours**.\n4. **Excluded:** Managerial, confidential staff, armed guards, railway school teachers. No statutory limit under HOER.\n- **Overtime:** Paid at 2 times the ordinary rate of wages for hours worked beyond statutory limits (under Section 132 of Railways Act & Factories Act).\n\n### 5. 7th CPC Pay Structure & MACP Scheme\n- **Pay Matrix:** Replaced Pay Bands & Grade Pay. 18 Levels. Fitment factor 2.57.\n- **Annual Increment:** 3% uniform rate granted on 1st January or 1st July depending on qualifying 6 months service.\n- **Modified Assured Career Progression (MACP):**\n  - Granted on completion of 10, 20, and 30 years of regular service without promotion.\n  - Financial upgradation to the immediate next Pay Level in the hierarchy.\n  - Requires benchmark of **'Very Good'** in APARs for last 5 years.\n",
