    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. Concepts of Manpower Planning & Rightsizing\nWith technological transformations (electrification, Electronic Interlocking, Vande Bharat trainsets, mechanized track maintenance, IT systems like FOIS and IPAS), manual jobs have become obsolete, requiring strategic redeployment and rightsizing.\n\n### 2. Post Classifications & Procedures\n- **Permanent Revenue Posts:** Sanctioned permanently against recurring operational/maintenance needs, funded from ordinary working expenses (Revenue).\n- **Temporary Revenue Posts:** Sanctioned for a limited duration (usually up to 1 year, extendable) for seasonal or temporary workloads.\n- **Workcharged Posts:**\n  - Created specifically against the approved estimate of a capital project/work (e.g., Construction of New Line, Doubling, Electrification).\n  - Salaries are debited to the capital estimate of that specific work.\n  - The post lapses as soon as the project is completed and commissioned. Cannot be retained indefinitely.\n\n### 3. Rules for Creation and Surrender of Posts\n- **Surrender of Posts:** Posts lying vacant for more than 2 years are deemed surrendered (silent surrender / abolished).\n- **Creation against New Assets:**\n  - GM has delegated powers to create safety category posts for new assets (e.g., new stations, signaling cabins, substations) with matching money-value surrenders.\n  - Non-safety post creations strictly require Railway Board / Ministry of Finance concurrence.\n- **Matching Surrender Formula:** To create a post of Grade Pay 4200 (Level 6), posts of equivalent monetary value in the vacancy bank must be surrendered.\n\n### 4. Benchmarking Indices\n- Maintained by the Efficiency and Research Directorate of the Railway Board.\n- Evaluates the lowest MPRK (Men Per Route Km) among all zones as the national benchmark.\n- Zones operating above the national benchmark are mandated to freeze recruitments and accelerate redeployment to bring operational costs down.\n",
