    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. The Standard Forms (SF) under RS (D&A) Rules, 1968\n| Form No. | Purpose | Trigger / Usage |\n|---|---|---|\n| **SF-1** | Order of Suspension | Placed under suspension during pending investigation or disciplinary proceedings (Rule 5(1)) |\n| **SF-2** | Deemed Suspension | Automatically issued when detained in custody exceeding **48 hours** (Rule 5(2)) |\n| **SF-3** | Certificate of Non-employment | Submitted by employee under suspension to claim Subsistence Allowance |\n| **SF-4** | Revocation of Suspension | Issued when suspension is terminated by competent authority |\n| **SF-5** | Charge-sheet for Major Penalty | For instituting major penalty proceedings under Rule 9; includes 4 annexures |\n| **SF-6** | Refusal of Inspection of Documents | When Disciplinary Authority refuses inspection on grounds of public interest |\n| **SF-7** | Appointment of Inquiry Officer (IO) | Appointing IO to conduct formal inquiry when employee denies charges in SF-5 |\n| **SF-8** | Appointment of Presenting Officer (PO) | Nominating an officer to present the administration's case before IO |\n| **SF-10** | Common Proceedings | When two or more railway servants are jointly charged in the same case |\n| **SF-11** | Charge-sheet for Minor Penalty | For instituting minor penalty proceedings under Rule 11 (requires 10-day response time) |\n| **SF-11(b)** | Dropping Major & Instituting Minor with Inquiry | Holding regular inquiry under Rule 11(1)(b) for minor penalty |\n\n### 2. Classification of Penalties (Rule 6)\n#### Minor Penalties:\n1. **Censure** (Formal reprimand recorded in service book).\n2. Withholding of promotion for a specified period.\n3. Recovery from pay of the whole or part of any pecuniary loss caused to Government by negligence.\n4. Withholding of Privilege Passes and/or PTOs.\n5. Reduction to a lower stage in the time-scale of pay for a period not exceeding 3 years, without cumulative effect and not adversely affecting pension.\n6. Withholding of increments of pay (without cumulative effect).\n\n#### Major Penalties:\n7. Withholding of increments with cumulative effect or reduction to a lower stage in time-scale with cumulative effect.\n8. Reduction to a lower time-scale of pay, grade, post, or service.\n9. **Compulsory Retirement:** Permitted with full or reduced pensionary benefits.\n10. **Removal from Service:** Disqualification from future government employment is NOT attached.\n11. **Dismissal from Service:** Mandatory disqualification from future government employment.\n\n### 3. Detailed Step-by-Step Major Penalty Procedure (Rule 9)\n```\n[Misconduct / Vigilance Report]\n              \u2502\n              \u25bc\n    Issue SF-5 (Major Penalty Charge Sheet)\n    (Annexure I: Articles of Charge\n     Annexure II: Statement of Imputations\n     Annexure III: List of Documents\n     Annexure IV: List of Witnesses)\n              \u2502\n              \u25bc Employee given 10 days to reply\n   \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n   \u25bc                     \u25bc\nCharges Admitted     Charges Denied / No Reply\n   \u2502                     \u2502\nDisciplinary Authority   \u25bc\nimposes penalty      Issue SF-7 (Appoint IO) & SF-8 (Appoint PO)\n                         \u2502\n                         \u25bc\n                     Preliminary Hearing -> Regular Hearing -> Examination of Witnesses\n                         \u2502\n                         \u25bc\n                     IO submits Inquiry Report (proves/disproves charges)\n                         \u2502\n                         \u25bc\n                     Copy of IO Report served to Charged Official (15 days to represent)\n                         \u2502\n                         \u25bc\n                     Disciplinary Authority passes Speaking Order\n```\n\n### 4. Special Provisions & Remedies\n- **Rule 14(ii):** Power to dispense with inquiry where the Disciplinary Authority is satisfied, for reasons recorded in writing, that it is not reasonably practicable to hold an inquiry in the manner provided in these rules.\n- **Subsistence Allowance (Rule 1303 IREC II):**\n  - First 3 months: 50% of basic pay + DA.\n  - Beyond 3 months: Can be increased by up to 50% (to 75%) if delay is not attributable to employee, or decreased by up to 50% (to 25%) if delay is caused by employee.\n- **Appeals (Rule 18-24):** Preferred within **45 days** of receipt of penalty order to the Appellate Authority.\n- **Revision (Rule 25):** Preferred within **6 months** to GM, PHOD, or Railway Board.\n",
