    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. Fundamental Canons of Conduct (Rule 3)\n- **Rule 3(1)(i):** Maintain absolute integrity.\n- **Rule 3(1)(ii):** Maintain devotion to duty.\n- **Rule 3(1)(iii):** Do nothing which is unbecoming of a railway servant.\n- **Rule 3A:** Promptness and courtesy in dealing with the public and colleagues.\n- **Rule 3B:** Observance of Government policies regarding marriage age, preservation of environment, prevention of crime against women.\n- **Rule 3C (Prevention of Sexual Harassment):**\n  - Strict prohibition of physical contact, sexual favors, sexually colored remarks, showing pornography, or unwelcome physical/verbal conduct.\n  - Every administrative office, division, and workshop must maintain an **Internal Complaints Committee (ICC)** headed by a senior woman officer.\n  - The ICC inquiry report is treated directly as an Inquiry Report under Rule 9 of RS (D&A) Rules.\n\n### 2. Restrictions on Political & Public Activities\n- **Rule 5:** Shall not be a member of any political party, nor take part in political elections, nor canvass votes.\n- **Rule 6 & 7:** Shall not own, edit, or manage any newspaper or radio/TV program, nor publish statements criticizing current policies of Central or State Government.\n- **Rule 9:** Unauthorised communication of official documents or operational information is strictly prohibited (official secrets).\n\n### 3. Financial Conduct, Gifts & Private Trade\n- **Rule 11 (Gifts):**\n  - A gift includes free transport, boarding, lodging, or pecuniary advantage.\n  - Casual meal, lift, or hospitality is not a gift.\n  - Near relatives and personal friends on weddings/anniversaries: Report to Government if value exceeds **Rs. 25,000** (Group A), **Rs. 15,000** (Group B), or **Rs. 7,500** (Group C).\n  - From other persons without official dealings: Prior sanction if exceeds **Rs. 5,000** (Group A/B) or **Rs. 2,000** (Group C).\n- **Rule 13 (Private Trade or Employment):**\n  - Cannot engage directly or indirectly in any trade or business, or undertake any other employment without previous sanction of the competent authority.\n  - Can undertake honorary social, charitable, or literary work without detriment to official duties.\n- **Rule 18 (Movable & Immovable Property):**\n  - Prior intimation / sanction required for purchasing or selling immovable property (land, house).\n  - Movable property transactions exceeding **two months' basic pay** must be reported to the administration within 30 days.\n  - Annual Immovable Property Return (AIPR / APR) is mandatory for Group A and B officers by **31st January** each year via SPARROW. Failure to submit denies vigilance clearance for promotion and empanelment.\n",
