    "key_concepts": [
      "Qualifying Service: Minimum 10 years for pension, minimum 5 years for retirement gratuity, 25 years for full UPS",
      "Pension Formula: 50% of last basic pay or 50% of average emoluments in last 10 months, whichever is higher",
      "Commutation: Up to 40% of basic pension, fully restored after 15 years",
      "Retirement Gratuity: 1/4th of monthly emoluments for each 6-month period, max 16.5 times pay, ceiling Rs. 20 Lakhs (raised to Rs. 25 Lakhs when DA crossed 50%)",
      "Family Pension: Normal rate 30% of pay; Enhanced rate 50% of pay for 10 years or up to age 67",
      "NPS: Defined contribution (10% employee + 14% government contribution) into PRAN Tier I account",
      "Unified Pension Scheme (UPS): Guaranteed pension 50% of last drawn pay, Rs. 10,000 min pension, 60% family pension, DR indexation"
    ],
    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. Pension Architecture & Qualifying Service\nUnder the Railway Services (Pension) Rules, 1993 (applicable to staff appointed prior to 01.01.2004):\n- **Qualifying Service (QS):** Service rendered after age 18 in permanent or temporary capacity followed without break by confirmation.\n- Minimum QS for Monthly Pension: **10 years** (20 half-yearly periods).\n- Minimum QS for Retirement Gratuity: **5 years**.\n- Calculation of Pension:\n  $$\\text{Basic Pension} = 50\\% \\times \\max(\\text{Last Basic Pay}, \\text{Average Emoluments of Last 10 Months})$$\n  - Minimum Pension: **Rs. 9,000/month** (under 7th CPC).\n  - Maximum Pension: **Rs. 1,25,000/month** (50% of highest pay Level 18 Rs. 2,50,000).\n\n### 2. Commutation of Pension & Gratuity\n- **Commutation of Pension:**\n  - Up to **40%** of basic pension can be commuted for a lump-sum payment.\n  - Formula: $\\text{Lump Sum} = 40\\% \\times \\text{Pension} \\times 12 \\times \\text{Commutation Factor}$ (based on age on next birthday).\n  - Restored to full pension after **15 years** from date of credit.\n- **Retirement Gratuity:**\n  $$\\text{Gratuity} = \\frac{\\text{Emoluments (Basic + DA)}}{4} \\times \\text{Number of completed 6-month periods}$$\n  - Maximum limit: 16.5 times the monthly emoluments.\n  - Statutory Ceiling: **Rs. 20 Lakhs** (automatically increased by 25% to **Rs. 25 Lakhs** when Dearness Allowance touched 50% in Jan 2024).\n- **Death Gratuity:** Paid to nominee if employee dies in harness based on progressive slabs (up to 33 times emoluments for >20 years service).\n\n### 3. Leave Encashment at Retirement\n- Lump sum payment for accumulated LAP + LHAP up to a maximum ceiling of **300 days**.\n- Formula: $\\text{Encashment} = \\frac{\\text{Pay} + \\text{DA}}{30} \\times \\text{Unutilized Leave Days}$.\n\n### 4. Comparison: OPS vs NPS vs UPS (Crucial for 2026/2027 Exam!)\n| Feature | Old Pension Scheme (OPS) | National Pension System (NPS) | Unified Pension Scheme (UPS) [New!] |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Applicability** | Joined before 01.01.2004 | Joined on or after 01.01.2004 | Option for all central/railway staff from 2025 |\n| **Type** | Defined Benefit (Non-contributory) | Defined Contribution (Market-linked) | Defined Assured Benefit (Contributory) |\n| **Employee Contribution** | Nil (GPF voluntary) | 10% of Pay + DA | 10% of Pay + DA |\n| **Govt Contribution** | Fully funded by Budget | 14% of Pay + DA | **18.5%** of Pay + DA |\n| **Assured Pension** | 50% of last pay / 10-mo average | No assurance (annuity dependent) | **50% of last 12-month average pay** (min 25 yrs service) |\n| **Minimum Pension** | Rs. 9,000 / month | Depends on corpus | **Rs. 10,000 / month** (min 10 yrs service) |\n| **Family Pension** | 30% of pay / 50% enhanced | Annuity dependent | **60% of pension of the employee** |\n| **Dearness Relief (DR)** | Yes (indexed to AICPI) | No (fixed annuity rate) | **Yes (indexed to inflation/AICPI)** |\n| **Lump Sum at Superannuation** | Gratuity + Encashment | 60% corpus tax-free + Gratuity | 1/10th of monthly pay+DA per 6 mo + Gratuity |\n",
    "deprecated_vs_modern": {
      "deprecated_practice": "Pure NPS without defined pension guarantee (faced widespread employee discontent); manual pension payment orders (PPO).",
      "modern_practice": "Unified Pension Scheme (UPS) approved in 2024 offering assured 50% pension with Dearness Relief; electronic PPO (e-PPO) generated via ARPAN and HRMS Settlement.",
      "transition_notes": "Candidates must clearly highlight the historic shift from OPS (1993 rules) -> NPS (2004) -> UPS (2024-2025 approval for 2025/2026 roll-out)."
    }
