    "id": "est_11",
    "section": "Establishment Rules",
    "page": "Page 2",
    "title": "11. IT in Railway Administration: HRMS, IPAS, e-Office & Portals",
    "subtitle": "HRMS Modules, IPAS Payroll & Accounting, LIMBS, ARPAN, CPGRAMS, ANUBHAV",
    "official_references": [
      "Railway Board HRMS Project Directives (CRIS)",
      "Accounts Directorate Manual on IPAS (Integrated Payroll & Accounting System)",
      "Department of Legal Affairs LIMBS Portal Guidelines",
      "DoPT & DARPG Guidelines on e-Office & CPGRAMS"
    ],
    "key_concepts": [
      "HRMS: Centralized cloud-native HR system developed by CRIS for all railway employees",
      "Key HRMS Modules: Employee Master, e-SR, Leave, e-Pass/PTO, Loan & Advances, APAR/SPARROW, Transfer, Settlement, UMID",
      "IPAS: Integrated Payroll and Accounting System replacing legacy PRIME/AFRES",
      "e-Office: NIC cloud system for paperless digital file movement, dak receipt, digital signatures",
      "LIMBS: Legal Information Management and Briefing System monitoring court cases",
      "ARPAN: Advanced Railway Pension Access Network automating pension revisions and PPO",
      "CPGRAMS & ANUBHAV: Public grievance monitoring and retiring employee achievements showcase"
    ],
    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. HRMS (Human Resource Management System) Architecture\nDeveloped and managed by CRIS (Centre for Railway Information Systems), HRMS has completely transformed railway personnel administration into a paperless, employee-centric digital environment:\n\n```\n                                  CRIS HRMS CLOUD\n                                         \u2502\n        \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n        \u25bc              \u25bc                 \u25bc                \u25bc              \u25bc\n     Employee        e-SR              Leave           e-Pass /        APAR /\n      Master        Module            Module             PTO          SPARROW\n  (Bio-data/UMID) (Service Book)   (Apply/Sanction)  (UPN / IRCTC)  (Digital Appr.)\n        \u2502              \u2502                 \u2502                \u2502              \u2502\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                                         \u25bc\n                             Settlement & e-PPO Engine\n                                         \u2502\n                                         \u25bc\n                             IPAS (Salary & Accounts)\n```\n\n#### Core Functional Modules of HRMS:\n1. **Employee Master & e-SR:**\n   - Single source of truth containing bio-data, family declarations, educational qualifications, service progression, promotions, awards, and punishments.\n   - Complete replacement of the legacy physical Service Book.\n2. **e-Pass / e-PTO Module:**\n   - Real-time generation of Unique Pass Number (UPN).\n   - Direct API integration with the CRIS PRS/IRCTC booking engine for paperless reservation.\n   - Supports split passes, family declaration updates, and online cancellation/re-issue.\n3. **Leave Module:**\n   - Online application, recommendation, and sanction of LAP, LHAP, CL, CCL, and Commuted leave.\n   - Real-time leave balance deduction and automatic feed to monthly IPAS attendance/salary.\n4. **Loans & Advances Module:** Online processing of PF Temporary Advance and PF Non-Refundable Withdrawal.\n5. **Office Order & Transfer Module:**\n   - Tracks inter-railway, inter-divisional, and mutual transfer requests transparently by chronological priority.\n6. **Settlement Module:**\n   - Automated processing of terminal dues for retiring staff.\n   - Integrates with ARPAN to generate digital e-PPO.\n7. **UMID (Unique Medical Identity Card):**\n   - QR-code enabled medical card for employees and dependents, accepted across all railway hospitals and empaneled private hospitals nationwide.\n\n### 2. IPAS (Integrated Payroll & Accounting System)\n- Replaced legacy decentralized systems (PRIME - Payroll & Related Information Management Employee-end, and AFRES - Advanced Financial & Railway Expenditure System).\n- Single, centralized web-based accounting engine running across all Zonal Railways and Production Units.\n- Automatically calculates:\n  - Basic Pay + Dearness Allowance (DA) + House Rent Allowance (HRA) + Transport Allowance (TPTA).\n  - Running Allowances (Kilometreage Allowance KMA) for Loco Pilots and Guards.\n  - Workshop Incentive Bonus (via WISE interface).\n  - Deductions: NPS (10%), GPF, Income Tax TDS, Professional Tax, Railway quarter rent, SBF.\n  - Direct electronic disbursement of salaries via RBI NEFT/RTGS into employee bank accounts on the last working day of the month.\n\n### 3. Specialized Portals: LIMBS, ARPAN, CPGRAMS, ANUBHAV\n- **LIMBS (Legal Information Management and Briefing System):**\n  - Web portal managed by Ministry of Law & Justice used across all railway zones.\n  - Tracks court cases in CAT, High Courts, and Supreme Court.\n  - Monitors filing of counter-affidavits, compliance of court orders, advocate fees, and contempt alerts.\n- **ARPAN (Advanced Railway Pension Access Network):**\n  - Centralized pension portal of Western Railway expanded nationwide.\n  - Holds historical pension data of over 1.5 million pensioners.\n  - Facilitates instant revision of pension upon pay commission implementation and handles pensioner grievances.\n- **CPGRAMS:** Department of Administrative Reforms & Public Grievances portal; allows public and railway employees to lodge grievances with mandatory 30-day resolution timeline.\n- **ANUBHAV Portal:** Platform initiated by the Department of Pension & Pensioners' Welfare enabling retiring railway servants to write a personal narrative/retrospective of their career accomplishments.\n",
    "deprecated_vs_modern": {
      "deprecated_practice": "PRIME and AFRES legacy software running on local decentralized servers; physical Service Registers; paper privilege passes with manual counterfoils.",
      "modern_practice": "Centralized cloud IPAS; CRIS HRMS with e-Pass, e-SR, online Leave and Settlement; paperless e-Office with digital DSC signatures.",
      "transition_notes": "PRIME and AFRES were completely phased out and replaced by IPAS. Physical pass issuance is virtually discontinued."
    }
