    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. The Four Streams of Railway Revenue\n```\n                          GROSS TRAFFIC RECEIPTS (GTR)\n                                        \u2502\n     \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n     \u25bc                      \u25bc                      \u25bc                      \u25bc\nGoods Earnings     Passenger Earnings    Other Coaching Earnings    Sundry Earnings\n(~65-70% of total)  (~25-30% of total)     (Parcels, Luggage,       (Land lease, scrap,\nCoal, iron ore,     PRS, UTS,              Postal haulage,          commercial ads,\ncement, containers  UTS Mobile             Special trains)          catering license)\n```\n\n### 2. The Station Balance Sheet\nEvery Station Master must submit a monthly **Station Balance Sheet** to the Traffic Accounts Office (TAO):\n- **Debits (What the station owes to Railways):**\n  - Opening balance of uncollected dues.\n  - Cash collected from passenger tickets (UTS, PRS).\n  - Freight collected on 'Paid' inward/outward consignments.\n  - Demurrage and wharfage charges accrued.\n  - Telegraph/miscellaneous earnings.\n- **Credits (Discharge of station liabilities):**\n  - Cash remitted into Cash Office or Government Treasury / Bank.\n  - Credit Notes (government warrants, military warrants).\n  - Vouchers, special concessions, and authorized refunds.\n  - Closing balance of outstandings (admissible outstandings).\n- **Discrepancies:** Handled through **Error Sheets** issued by the Traffic Accounts Office to recover uncollected revenue from station staff.\n\n### 3. The Traffic Book & Revenue Apportionment\n- **Traffic Book:** Compiled in 4 Parts:\n  - *Part A:* Station Accounts (Debits, credits, cash in transit).\n  - *Part B:* Cash Remittances and adjustments.\n  - *Part C:* Apportionment of Through Traffic Earnings among Zonal Railways.\n  - *Part D:* Summary of Gross Traffic Earnings and Suspense Balances.\n- **Apportionment Principles:** When a freight rake travels from East Coast Railway (Bhubaneswar) to Northern Railway (Delhi) passing through South Eastern and North Central Railways, the total freight paid is divided among the 4 zones in proportion to the route kilometer distance traversed in each zone.\n",
