    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. Comparative Analysis: C&AG vs CGA (High-Frequency Exam Question!)\n| Parameter | Comptroller & Auditor General (C&AG) | Controller General of Accounts (CGA) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Constitutional Status** | Independent Constitutional Authority (**Article 148**) | Statutory / Executive Office under Ministry of Finance |\n| **Department** | Head of Indian Audit and Accounts Department (IA&AD) | Head of Indian Civil Accounts Organisation (Department of Expenditure) |\n| **Primary Role** | **External Audit** of all receipts and expenditures of Union & States | **Accounting & Internal Financial Reporting** for Union Government |\n| **Reporting Line** | Reports directly to the **President of India** / Parliament | Reports to the **Finance Minister** / Secretary (Expenditure) |\n| **Removal Process** | Same as a Supreme Court Judge (proved misbehavior/incapacity via impeachment) | Regular civil service conditions |\n| **Railway Connection** | Conducts statutory audit through **Principal Director of Audit (PDA)** | Manages Public Financial Management System (**PFMS**); coordinates national accounts |\n\n### 2. Powers and Duties of the C&AG (Act of 1971)\n- Under Articles 149-151 and the C&AG Act of 1971:\n  1. Audits all expenditure from the Consolidated Fund of India, Contingency Fund, and Public Account.\n  2. Audits all trading, manufacturing, profit and loss accounts, and balance sheets of government departments and public undertakings.\n  3. Conducts **Performance Audits**, **Financial Audits**, and **Compliance Audits** of Indian Railways.\n  4. Has absolute right of access to all books, vouchers, documents, and digital databases (e.g., read-only access to IPAS, FOIS, and PRS).\n\n### 3. Role of the Principal Director of Audit (PDA) in Railways\n- Stationed at the Zonal Headquarters of each of the 17 Zonal Railways.\n- Heads the statutory Railway Audit team.\n- Issues Audit Notes, Part I/II Inspection Reports, Special Letters, and Draft Paras to the General Manager and Railway Board.\n- Vets the Appropriation Accounts compiled by the Principal Financial Adviser (PFA).\n",
