    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. The OSI 7-Layer Model vs TCP/IP Suite\n```\n     OSI LAYER             PDU              PRIMARY PROTOCOLS / DEVICES\n  7. Application         Data         HTTP/HTTPS, DNS, SMTP, FTP, SSH, SNMP\n  6. Presentation        Data         SSL/TLS, JPEG, ASCII, Encryption/Compression\n  5. Session             Data         NetBIOS, RPC, Session Management\n  \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  4. Transport          Segment       TCP (connection-oriented), UDP (connectionless)\n  3. Network            Packet        IP (IPv4/IPv6), ICMP, ARP, OSPF, BGP / Routers\n  2. Data Link           Frame        Ethernet (802.3), Wi-Fi (802.11), PPP / Switches\n  1. Physical             Bits        Cables (Cat6, Optical Fiber), Hubs, Repeaters\n```\n\n### 2. TCP 3-Way Handshake & Connection Teardown\n- **Establishment (3-Way Handshake):**\n  1. Client sends `SYN` (Sequence Number = $x$).\n  2. Server responds with `SYN-ACK` (Sequence Number = $y$, Acknowledgment = $x + 1$).\n  3. Client sends `ACK` (Sequence Number = $x + 1$, Acknowledgment = $y + 1$). Connection established!\n- **Termination (4-Way Teardown):**\n  1. Initiator sends `FIN`.\n  2. Receiver sends `ACK`.\n  3. Receiver sends `FIN`.\n  4. Initiator sends `ACK` and enters `TIME_WAIT` state (typically 2 MSL) before closing.\n\n### 3. IP Addressing, Subnetting & CIDR\n- **IPv4 Address:** 32 bits divided into 4 octets. Classes A, B, C, D (Multicast), E (Reserved).\n- **Subnet Mask:** Distinguishes Network bits from Host bits.\n- **CIDR (Classless Inter-Domain Routing):** E.g., `192.168.1.0/24` -> Subnet mask `255.255.255.0`, 256 addresses (254 usable hosts: $2^{32-24} - 2$).\n- **Private IP Ranges (RFC 1918):**\n  - Class A: `10.0.0.0` to `10.255.255.255` (`10.0.0.0/8`)\n  - Class B: `172.16.0.0` to `172.31.255.255` (`172.16.0.0/12`)\n  - Class C: `192.168.0.0` to `192.168.255.255` (`192.168.0.0/16`)\n\n### 4. Railway Enterprise Network Architecture (Railnet)\n- Indian Railways operates **Railnet**, an extensive nationwide IP network managed by **RailTel** and CRIS:\n  - Connects Railway Board, 17 Zonal HQs, 68 Divisions, Production Units, Workshops, and Stations.\n  - Optical Fiber Cable (OFC) runs along railway tracks covering over 60,000+ route kilometers.\n  - Uses **MPLS-VPN** (Multi-Protocol Label Switching) to isolate sensitive operational traffic (Signaling, PRS, FOIS) from general office internet traffic.\n",
