    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. Data Flow Diagrams (DFD) vs Unified Modeling Language (UML)\n- **DFDs (Structured Analysis):**\n  - Focuses on the flow of data through processes.\n  - **Context Diagram (Level 0):** High-level view showing the entire system as a single process interacting with external entities.\n  - **Level 1 DFD:** Decomposes the system into major functional sub-processes and data stores.\n  - **Level 2 DFD:** Drills down into complex sub-processes.\n- **UML (Object-Oriented Design):**\n  - **Use Case Diagram:** Shows system boundaries, actors, use cases, `<<include>>` (mandatory) and `<<extend>>` (optional) relationships.\n  - **Class Diagram:** Visualizes classes, attributes, methods, associations, aggregation (weak), composition (strong), and generalization (inheritance).\n  - **Sequence Diagram:** Shows interaction between objects arranged in time sequence (Lifelines, Messages, Activation bars).\n\n### 2. SOAP vs REST Web Services\n| Feature | SOAP (Simple Object Access Protocol) | REST (Representational State Transfer) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Protocol / Style** | Strict Protocol with formal specification | Architectural style based on HTTP |\n| **Data Format** | Strictly **XML** | Lightweight **JSON**, XML, Plain text, HTML |\n| **Transport** | Independent (HTTP, SMTP, TCP, JMS) | Strictly uses **HTTP / HTTPS** |\n| **Contract** | Formal **WSDL** (Web Services Description Language) | Informal / OpenAPI / Swagger specification |\n| **State** | Can be stateful or stateless | Strictly **Stateless** |\n| **Performance** | Slower, heavy parsing overhead | Fast, lightweight, caching supported |\n| **Security** | WS-Security (message-level encryption) | HTTPS / TLS, OAuth 2.0, JWT tokens |\n",
