    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. 2D Transformation Matrices (Homogeneous Coordinates)\nPoints represented as $\\begin{bmatrix} x & y & 1 \\end{bmatrix}^T$:\n- **Translation:**\n  $$\\begin{bmatrix} x' \\\\ y' \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & t_x \\\\ 0 & 1 & t_y \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}$$\n- **Rotation (about origin by angle $\\theta$):**\n  $$\\begin{bmatrix} x' \\\\ y' \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} \\cos\\theta & -\\sin\\theta & 0 \\\\ \\sin\\theta & \\cos\\theta & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}$$\n- **Scaling:**\n  $$\\begin{bmatrix} x' \\\\ y' \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} s_x & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & s_y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}$$\n\n### 2. CNC Programming: Essential G-Codes & M-Codes in Workshops\nUsed extensively in Railway Production Units (ICF Perambur, RCF Kapurthala, BLW Varanasi, RWF Yelahanka):\n| Code | Function / Purpose | Application in Railway Manufacturing |\n|---|---|---|\n| **G00** | Rapid positioning (non-cutting motion at rapid traverse) | Moving tool close to wheel axle blank |\n| **G01** | Linear interpolation (cutting motion at controlled feed rate) | Straight turning of axle journal |\n| **G02** | Circular interpolation clockwise (CW) | Machining wheel flange radius |\n| **G03** | Circular interpolation counter-clockwise (CCW) | Machining wheel tread profile curve |\n| **G20 / G21** | Imperial (inches) / Metric (millimeters) input | Setting workshop coordinate units |\n| **G28** | Return to machine reference point / home | End of machining cycle |\n| **G90 / G91** | Absolute positioning / Incremental positioning | Coordinate reference frame selection |\n| **M00 / M01** | Program stop / Optional stop | Operator inspection of workpiece |\n| **M03 / M04** | Spindle start CW / Spindle start CCW | Starting wheel lathe headstock spindle |\n| **M05** | Spindle stop | Stopping spindle rotation |\n| **M08 / M09** | Coolant ON / Coolant OFF | Flooding cutting zone with soluble oil |\n| **M30** | Program end and rewind | End of CNC part cycle |\n\n### 3. Finite Element Analysis (FEA) in Railway Engineering\n- **Structural Integrity:** Simulating crashworthiness of LHB and Vande Bharat coach shells under 1500 kN compressive buffing loads.\n- **Dynamic Stress Analysis:** Bogie frames, wheelsets, rail joints subjected to cyclic dynamic fatigue loads.\n- **Thermal FEA:** Heat dissipation on disc brakes during emergency braking from 160 km/h.\n",
