    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. Data Centre Tiers (Uptime Institute Classification)\n| Parameter | Tier I (Basic) | Tier II (Redundant) | Tier III (Concurrently Maintainable) | Tier IV (Fault Tolerant) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Availability** | **99.671%** | **99.741%** | **99.982%** | **99.995%** |\n| **Annual Downtime** | Up to 28.8 hours | Up to 22.0 hours | Up to **1.6 hours** | Up to **26.3 minutes** |\n| **Redundancy** | $N$ (No redundancy) | $N + 1$ capacity | $N + 1$ (Dual power paths, 1 active) | **$2(N + 1)$** (Dual active paths) |\n| **Maintenance** | Requires shutdown | Requires shutdown | **Zero planned downtime** | **Zero planned downtime** |\n| **Fault Tolerance** | Vulnerable to events | Vulnerable to events | Vulnerable to unplanned events | **Withstands worst-case failure** |\n\n### 2. HVAC & Hot Aisle / Cold Aisle Containment\n```\n   [Cold Aisle Containment: 18-22\u00b0C Air delivered through perforated tiles]\n               \u2502                                      \u2502\n               \u25bc Cool air in                          \u25bc Cool air in\n        \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510                        \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n        \u2502 Server Rack \u2502                        \u2502 Server Rack \u2502\n        \u2502 Front Inflow\u2502                        \u2502 Front Inflow\u2502\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2524                        \u251c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2524\n        \u2502 Exhaust Out \u2502                        \u2502 Exhaust Out \u2502\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518                        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n               \u25b2                                      \u25b2\n               \u2502 Hot exhaust air (32-38\u00b0C)             \u2502 Hot exhaust air (32-38\u00b0C)\n   [Hot Aisle Containment: Hot air extracted back into ceiling plenum to PAC units]\n```\n- Prevents mixing of supply and exhaust air, slashing HVAC power consumption and preventing localized server hot spots.\n\n### 3. Backup 3-2-1 Rule & Disaster Recovery Metrics\n- **The 3-2-1 Backup Rule:**\n  - Maintain at least **3** copies of critical data.\n  - Store backups across at least **2** different storage media (e.g., NVMe SAN arrays and LTO Magnetic Tape).\n  - Keep at least **1** copy completely **offsite** (at a remote Disaster Recovery Center or secure cloud).\n- **Disaster Recovery Metrics:**\n  - **Recovery Point Objective (RPO):** Maximum acceptable age of data lost during disaster (e.g., RPO = 5 minutes means at most 5 minutes of transaction data lost).\n  - **Recovery Time Objective (RTO):** Maximum allowable time to restore service after disruption (e.g., RTO = 30 minutes).\n- **Indian Railways / CRIS DR Centre:**\n  - Primary Data Centre: **CRIS Chanakyapuri, New Delhi**.\n  - Secondary Disaster Recovery Centre (DRC): **Secunderabad**.\n  - High-speed dedicated fiber link continuously synchronizes database transaction logs via Oracle Data Guard.\n",
