    "detailed_notes": "\n### 1. XML Parsers: DOM vs SAX\n| Feature | Document Object Model (DOM) | Simple API for XML (SAX) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Parsing Mechanism** | Tree-based model | Event-driven streaming model |\n| **Memory Footprint** | Loads entire XML document into RAM | Minimal; processes node by node as stream |\n| **Speed** | Slower for massive XML files | Very fast |\n| **Traversal** | Bidirectional (can navigate up and down tree) | Forward-only (single pass) |\n| **Modification** | Can insert, delete, modify XML nodes | Read-only stream (cannot modify in-place) |\n| **Best Used For** | Small/medium XML with complex cross-references | Massive XML data feeds (e.g., large train schedule feeds) |\n\n### 2. Secure Web Development in PHP\n- **Preventing SQL Injection (Use PDO Prepared Statements):**\n```php\n// INSECURE (Vulnerable to SQL Injection):\n$sql = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '\" . $_POST['user'] . \"'\";\n\n// SECURE (PDO Prepared Statement with Bound Parameters):\n$stmt = $pdo->prepare(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = :username\");\n$stmt->execute(['username' => $_POST['user']]);\n$user = $stmt->fetch();\n```\n- **Preventing Cross-Site Scripting (XSS):**\n  - Always sanitize output using `htmlspecialchars($input, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')`.\n- **Preventing Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF):**\n  - Generate cryptographically secure random token in `$_SESSION['csrf_token']` and validate on every POST request.\n\n### 3. Open Source Web CMS Systems in Government & Railways\n1. **Liferay Portal:**\n   - Java/J2EE-based enterprise portal framework.\n   - Built-in role-based access control (RBAC), portlet architecture (JSR-286), document management, single sign-on (SSO).\n   - **Indian Railways Adoption:** Extensively used in **Railnet internal zonal intranet portals** and CRIS enterprise portals.\n2. **Drupal:**\n   - Highly secure, modular PHP-based CMS favored for mission-critical government portals (e.g., Whitehouse, data.gov.in).\n   - Strict adherence to accessibility and granular user permissions.\n3. **WordPress:**\n   - Powers over 40% of the world's websites.\n   - User-friendly, vast ecosystem of plugins and themes; requires diligent patching to prevent security vulnerabilities.\n4. **Joomla:**\n   - Mid-tier PHP CMS between WordPress simplicity and Drupal complexity.\n",
